# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Development and test dependencies (direct only).
#
# Deliberately NOT installed into the production image — see Dockerfile.backend,
# which installs requirements.txt only. Shipping pytest and ruff to production
# adds attack surface and image size for tooling that never runs there.
#
# `-c requirements.txt` constrains this resolution to the versions already
# locked for runtime, so installing dev deps can never silently upgrade a
# runtime package out from under the locked set.
#
# Regenerate with:
#     pip-compile requirements-dev.in -o requirements-dev.txt
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-c requirements.txt

